WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.620
The London borough of Brent, 2021.

2
00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:08.430
56.1 per cent of its residents
were born outside the UK.

3
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.370
Across London, the share is 40.6 per cent,

4
00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:14.870
up from 36.7 in 2011.

5
00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:16.390
Now zoom out.

6
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:22.030
Of about 7,000 documented languages,
nearly half are considered endangered.

7
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:28.120
Without intervention, at least 1,500
could stop being spoken by 2100.

8
00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:31.830
Is the world becoming more
alike, or more diverse?

9
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.550
Or has nothing changed?

10
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.910
In this mission, you'll measure
diversity with Simpson's index,

11
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.370
and find out what is
linked to language loss.

12
00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:43.530
Then you'll test the idea
of cultural imperialism,

13
00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:47.190
from Europe's cinemas to
Netflix's non-English list.

14
00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:52.110
Your mission: decide whether the world
is becoming more alike or more diverse.
